DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Removal of Automatic Extensions for Certain E
 mployment Authorization Documents
DESCRIPTION:On October 30\, 2025\, DHS published an interim final rule (IF
 R) that amended DHS regulations to end the practice of automatically exten
 ding the validity of employment authorization documents (Forms I- 766 or E
 ADs) for aliens who have timely filed an application to renew their EAD in
  certain employment authorization categories. This final rule responds to 
 comments received on the IFR and reaffirms and finalizes the provisions of
  the IFR. Ending the automatic extension of EADs enhances benefit integrit
 y and prioritizes the proper vetting and screening of aliens before granti
 ng a new period of employment authorization and/or a new EAD.\nhttps://www
 .federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/14/2026-20955/removal-of-automatic-
 extensions-for-certain-employment-authorization-documents
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/14/2026-20955/remova
 l-of-automatic-extensions-for-certain-employment-authorization-documents
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
